   },
   {
    "id": 1023301,
    "guid": "13059F10EF0211EA8C509F5B7AE9A43F",
    "previous_id": 1023300,
    "previous_guid": "F816C8F0EF0111EA8C509F5B7AE9A43F",
    "section": "<p>Test Procedure</p>",
    "section_color": "#E57785",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": true,
    "step": "Still squeezing, place the pipette tip into the test buffer vial.",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 41618,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "8.2",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 1023302,
    "guid": "192946D0EF0211EA8C509F5B7AE9A43F",
    "previous_id": 1023301,
    "previous_guid": "13059F10EF0211EA8C509F5B7AE9A43F",
    "section": "<p>Test Procedure</p>",
    "section_color": "#E57785",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": true,
    "step": "With the pipette tip still in the test buffer vial, slowly release the pressure on the bulb of the transfer pipette. NOTE: some liquid will flow into the lower bulb of the pipette \u2013 this is okay!",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 41618,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "8.3",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 1023304,
    "guid": "323AF880EF0211EA8C509F5B7AE9A43F",
    "previous_id": 1023302,
    "previous_guid": "192946D0EF0211EA8C509F5B7AE9A43F",
    "section": "<p>Test Procedure</p>",
    "section_color": "#E57785",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": true,
    "step": "Remove the pipette from the test buffer and place the pipette tip into the reaction tube.",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 41618,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "8.4",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 1023305,
    "guid": "3A4624F0EF0211EA8C509F5B7AE9A43F",
    "previous_id": 1023304,
    "previous_guid": "323AF880EF0211EA8C509F5B7AE9A43F",
    "section": "<p>Test Procedure</p>",
    "section_color": "#E57785",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": true,
    "step": "Firmly but slowly squeeze the top bulb of the pipette to empty the contents of the 40 microliter fixed volume pipette into the reaction tube. STILL SQUEEZING, remove the pipette from the reaction tube.\n 40 \u00b5L, or 1 fixed volume transfer pipette  \n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 41618,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "8.5",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 1023306,
    "guid": "41547AD0EF0211EA8C509F5B7AE9A43F",
    "previous_id": 1023305,
    "previous_guid": "3A4624F0EF0211EA8C509F5B7AE9A43F",
    "section": "<p>Test Procedure</p>",
    "section_color": "#E57785",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "Note: The fixed-volume transfer pipette is designed to collect an excess of liquid sample and dispense the correct volume of liquid sample into the reaction tube. Do not try to add fluid left in the lower \u201coverflow\u201d reservoir to the reaction tube. Discard the pipette in the biohazard waste.",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 41618,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "9",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 1023307,
    "guid": "4BBC34E0EF0211EA8C509F5B7AE9A43F",
    "previous_id": 1023306,
    "previous_guid": "41547AD0EF0211EA8C509F5B7AE9A43F",
    "section": "<p>Test Procedure</p>",
    "section_color": "#E57785",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "Screw the cap back onto the vial of test buffer. Discard this in the biohazardous waste.",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 41618,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "10",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 1023308,
    "guid": "5363BD80EF0211EA8C509F5B7AE9A43F",
    "previous_id": 1023307,
    "previous_guid": "4BBC34E0EF0211EA8C509F5B7AE9A43F",
    "section": "<p>Test Procedure</p>",
    "section_color": "#E57785",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "Close the reaction tube.\n**Do not** **place the sample into the heater/reader unit of the instrument until all samples for this run are ready.** Samples should be placed in the wells at the same time and the lid should be closed immediately to start the test run.\u00a0",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 41618,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "11",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 1023310,
    "guid": "57D1ED10EF0211EA8C509F5B7AE9A43F",
    "previous_id": 1023308,
    "previous_guid": "5363BD80EF0211EA8C509F5B7AE9A43F",
    "section": "<p>Test Procedure</p>",
    "section_color": "#E57785",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "If you only intend to run one sample, you may proceed to the onscreen instructions on the Harmony instrument. Otherwise, set this sample in the **sample queue block **and repeat the &#34;Test Procedure&#34; section for each additional sample.\u00a0Do NOT set the sample in the heater/reader until you are ready to start the run.\n\nBe sure to change gloves for each sample, and before using the touch screen on the instrument.\n\ngo to step #6  \n",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 41618,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "12",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   },
   {
    "id": 1023338,
    "guid": "9F14C3E0EF0311EA8C509F5B7AE9A43F",
    "previous_id": 1023310,
    "previous_guid": "57D1ED10EF0211EA8C509F5B7AE9A43F",
    "section": "<p>On-Screen Instructions</p>",
    "section_color": "#EA94FF",
    "section_duration": 0,
    "is_substep": false,
    "step": "The Harmony touch screen display will guide you through the steps to load the samples into the instrument. The software supports three methods of sample identification: manual text entry of an alphanumeric sample ID, photographing a barcode that can be read by instrument software, or photographing the patient directly. Please choose the method most suited to your institution\u2019s sample tracking systems and compliant with your institution\u2019s privacy and data security guidelines.",
    "data": null,
    "protocol_id": 41618,
    "case_id": 0,
    "critical_ids": "",
    "duration": 0,
    "original_id": 0,
    "number": "13",
    "cases": [],
    "critical": null
   }
